Feature: Compliance Rules
  Each compliance and surveillance rule can be switched off live from the
  Console. The change is saved as an override and survives a page reload.
  Scenario Outline: Switching a rule off takes effect and is saved -- @1.1  
    Given the Compliance Rules page is open with "wash_trading" active
    When I switch "wash_trading" off
    Then "wash_trading" shows as "Disabled"
    And the override for "wash_trading" was saved as disabled
    And after reloading the page "wash_trading" still shows as "Disabled"

  Scenario Outline: Switching a rule off takes effect and is saved -- @1.2  
    Given the Compliance Rules page is open with "missing_client_id" active
    When I switch "missing_client_id" off
    Then "missing_client_id" shows as "Disabled"
    And the override for "missing_client_id" was saved as disabled
    And after reloading the page "missing_client_id" still shows as "Disabled"

Feature: FixFlux Console navigation
  The Console's three tabs share one header. Each tab opens its own page and
  is the only tab marked as the current page.
  Scenario Outline: Each tab opens its page and is the active tab -- @1.1  
    Given I open the FixFlux Console at "/"
    When I click the "Compliance Rules" tab
    Then the "Compliance Rules" tab is the active tab
    And the page heading reads "Compliance & Surveillance Rules"

  Scenario Outline: Each tab opens its page and is the active tab -- @1.2  
    Given I open the FixFlux Console at "/"
    When I click the "Market Data" tab
    Then the "Market Data" tab is the active tab
    And the page heading reads "Live Market Data"

  Scenario Outline: Each tab opens its page and is the active tab -- @1.3  
    Given I open the FixFlux Console at "/market-data"
    When I click the "Fix Msg Injector" tab
    Then the "Fix Msg Injector" tab is the active tab
    And the page heading reads "FIX Message Test Injector"

Feature: Fix Msg Injector
  Raw FIX New Order Single lines pasted into the injector are parsed and
  published to the raw_orders topic, and the page reports the outcome.
  Scenario Outline: Valid FIX orders are published -- @1.1  
    Given the Fix Msg Injector page is open
    When I paste 1 valid New Order Single lines for "AAPL" and submit
    Then the injector status reads "1/1 published, 0 rejected."
    And 1 results are marked as published
    And 1 orders for "AAPL" were sent to raw_orders

  Scenario Outline: Valid FIX orders are published -- @1.2  
    Given the Fix Msg Injector page is open
    When I paste 3 valid New Order Single lines for "EURUSD" and submit
    Then the injector status reads "3/3 published, 0 rejected."
    And 3 results are marked as published
    And 3 orders for "EURUSD" were sent to raw_orders

Feature: Market Data
  The Market Data tab streams snapshots from market-data-api over a WebSocket
  and shows one row per symbol, formatted to the instrument's price level.
  Scenario Outline: A streamed snapshot appears as a formatted row -- @1.1  
    Given the Market Data page is open and the stream is live
    When a snapshot for "AAPL" with bid 174.9 and ask 175.1 arrives
    Then the "AAPL" row shows bid "174.90", ask "175.10" and mid "175.00"
    And the waiting message is hidden
    And the update counter reads "1 update"

  Scenario Outline: A streamed snapshot appears as a formatted row -- @1.2  
    Given the Market Data page is open and the stream is live
    When a snapshot for "EURUSD" with bid 1.0899 and ask 1.0901 arrives
    Then the "EURUSD" row shows bid "1.08990", ask "1.09010" and mid "1.09000"
    And the waiting message is hidden
    And the update counter reads "1 update"

